I've an separate partition (sda1) where linload.exe and
milo is located.

[super@alphalin super]$ df -h
Filesystem            Size  Used Avail Use% Mounted on
/dev/sda6             760M  104M  618M  14% /
/dev/sda2              17M  5.5M   11M  34% /boot
/dev/sdb1            1014M  579M  383M  60% /usr
/dev/sda1             1.4M  441k  982k  31% /mnt/sda1

/dev/sda1 is only temprorary mounted.

[super@alphalin super]$ ls -l -h /mnt/sda1
total 441k
-rwxrwxr-x    1 root     root         7.0k Oct 14  1998 linload.exe
-rwxrwxr-x    1 root     root         434k Apr 20  1999 milo

To start Linload from alphabios you have to add/modify the boot selection.
My configuration is:

LOADIDENTIFIER=Milo
SYSTEMPARTITION=scsi(0)disk(0)rdisk(0)partition(1)
OSLOADER=scsi(0)disk(0)rdisk(0)partition(1)\linload.exe
OSLOADPARTITION=scsi(0)disk(0)rdisk(0)partition(1)
OSLOADFILENAME=\
OSLOADOPTIONS=boot sda2:/vmlinuz-2.2.14-6.0 root=/dev/sda6

With this configuration linload starts milo and boot the kernel.
Take care that you have to modify the OSLOADOPTIONS entry to meet your
specific kernel in boot-dir and the root-dir at the end of the line.

