Are you using the original RH 7.0 kernel, 2.2.17-4 or whatever it
was?  At least on a UP2000, that kernel has a serious problem
with the PCI bus.  The X server tries to find out whether there
are more than two PCI buses, and the kernel gives a wrong answer,
which crashes the X server very hard.

The latest kernel, 2.2.19-7.0.1 seems to work for my system.  It
also has some security fixes.

(The great people at Harddata helped me resolve that problem.)

Good luck.

