You are probably having the same problem I had when installing SuSE 7.0 from
CD to my XL300.  The install would go fine, but I could not boot from the hard
disk when finished.  My XL300 will not boot from the CD.  I had to create a
boot diskette using the images from the CD.  So, I booted originally using a
diskette.

My XL300 would not run milo 2.0, so I had to boot using the older milo (1.2, I
believe).  I created a small DOS partition to place milo and linload in order
to boot from the hard disk using the AlphaBIOS menu.  When the installation
program runs, it is supposed to put milo and linload on this partition and,
like magic, the installation boots next time.  Unfortunately, the distribution
is not smart enough to know to put the older milo on the partition when you
boot with the older milo.  So, it puts milo 2.0 on there and you can't boot.

The solution is to manually copy milo and linload to the small DOS partition.

I don't recall the particulars of how I did that.  It involved logging in as
root BEFORE ending the installation and copying the files from the boot
diskette to the partition.

If you need more specific information, please write me individually and I will
see if I can recall exactly how it was done.  It did work, however.

Andy Seila
Bogart,  Georgia

