Shameman;

You might look into a couple tricks.  To get into the SRM all you need
to do is hit CTL C when you machine steps past the system check "the
number/letter combination thats at the top of the screen when you power
it on" 
Next you type "show dev" to see what you have for devices. 


Next you can put in a boot command to the SRM that looks like this. 

b dka400 -fi /kernels/vmlinux.gz -fl "root=/dev/scd0 \
initrd=images/ramdisk.img"

This should have you up and running in the install


