Alpha computers do not have "plug and pray" for ISA cards.
You need to configure them manually with 'ISACFG' command from the console
prompt >>>ISACFG -slot # -dev #... , etc.
You'll need to know what each card's IRQ, DMA, Memory Address & slot # in the
backplane.  Type typing >>>HELP ISACFG if you have any questions, or go to the
Compaq website, and dig into the database or ask the Wizard.  It's all there.

Good luck!

Tom C.

