> having
> is that XWindows loads automatically on boot.  I've been trying to figure
> out how to keep it from loading, but haven't figured it out.  Can anybody
> point me in the right direction?
> 
> Thanks
> 
> 
> 
> 
The way Debian works (and this is slightly different from RedHat-based
distros) is that the default is to boot into runlevel 2.  If you look in
/etc/rc2.d you should see something like S99xdm, which is symbolic
link to /etc/init.d/xdm which, in turn, is a script that fires up the
X display manager.  (Rather than xdm you might have one of
the other display managers, gdm, kdm, wdm.)  Removing the
symlink will cause the display manager, and the X window system,
not to start up automatically on boot-up.

Regards,
Martin Gelfand
Dept of Physics, Colorado State




