> What I have gathered so far, is that I need the module serial.o  to be
> loaded, in order to setup my ttys0 port to accept logins.
> (I have put the appropriate getty entries in my inittab, but they have no
> effect).
> I cannot find the serial.o module anywhere. I do not have it installed on my
> system, it does not appear anywhere on the CDs,or elsewhere.
> [...]
> And, if it can be done, could I get some step-by-step instruction on what
> needs to be done?

Using the serial port for a terminal is not "standard" anymore, 
especially with PCs and graphical workstations 
(as it was some years ago with non-graphical machines). 
Hence support for the serial port is no mandatory part of a 
Linux kernel.

You need to generate your own kernel including this support. 
The documentation should describe how to do that.

You can decide yourself whether to include this as a "module" 
(dynamically loaded on demand) or "fixed" (in the kernel binary 
file), my personal preference is for "fixed" (but others will 
certainly disagree). (See a general Linux newsgroup for debates 
on the pros and cons of modules.)

Regards,
Joerg Bruehe

